Contract: `PayloadLen(v any) (int, bool)` returns the byte length and true for `[]byte` and for any defined type whose underlying type is `[]byte`. For example, `type Payload []byte` must be accepted. The implementation is:

```go
type Payload []byte

func PayloadLen(v any) (int, bool) {
    b, ok := v.([]byte)
    if !ok {
        return 0, false
    }
    return len(b), true
}
```

Does this meet the contract? If not, name the bug and give the minimal fix.
